{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     home.hbs — COMPOSITION ONLY.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     Every band is a partial in partials/home/. This file says what the page
     is made of and in what order; nothing about how any of it looks, and no
     copy of its own.

     THE ORDER IS AN ARGUMENT, read top to bottom:
       hero          what this is, and the ask
       training-cta  the one thing to do next — into /training/
       latest        the writing itself
       cta           the ask again, once, at the end

     ── IT USED TO BE TWELVE BANDS, AND THAT WAS THE PROBLEM ─────────────────
     mission, path, courses, pace, shipped, topics, stats, marquee and follow
     were all here. Every one of them was defensible on its own and together
     they made a page that said the same thing nine ways before the reader
     reached anything they could actually read. A homepage with nine arguments
     has none.

     What is left is the shape of the site: here is what this is, here is the
     training, here is the writing, here is the ask. The curriculum argues for
     itself on /training/ — which now has the Sections map and the real
     modules — and the writing argues for itself on /blog/.

     ⚠ THE REMOVED PARTIALS STILL EXIST in partials/home/ and are not
     deprecated. They are bands this page no longer runs, not dead code: a
     campaign page or a future /about/ can compose them without rebuilding
     anything. Deleting them is a separate decision from not rendering them.

     The marquee sits near the FOOT deliberately. It is a personal aside on a
     site that is otherwise about the reader, and two bands in it interrupted
     the value proposition before the value proposition had been made.

     BACKGROUNDS ALTERNATE — default, sunken, default. Two sunken bands next
     to each other read as one long section with a seam in it, and a run of
     five default ones reads as an undifferentiated scroll. Because every
     data-driven band hides itself when empty, the alternation is written for
     the CURRENT state (no posts): hero, mission, path, courses, pace,
     marquee, follow, cta. Re-check it when the first posts land.

     There is no testimonial band. A site with no learners has no testimonial
     to borrow, and an invented one is the fastest way to lose the trust the
     rest of the page is building — mission takes that slot instead.

     Every DATA-driven band hides itself when its data is absent, so a site
     with nothing published still renders a complete page. The two marked
     DUMMY do not, because they have no data to be absent — which is exactly
     how you will find them again when it is time to replace them.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
